{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ys7ad1t2uqUpoY1wCHyXT","type":"tool_result","content":"# Kubernetes Well-Known Labels and Taints - Targeted Entries\n\n**1. `kubernetes.io/hostname`**\n- Used on: Node\n- Description: \"The Kubelet populates this label with the hostname of the node.\"\n\n**2. `topology.kubernetes.io/zone`**\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- Description: \"A zone represents a logical failure domain\" used by the kubelet or cloud-controller-manager.\n\n**3. `topology.kubernetes.io/region`**\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- Description: \"See topology.kubernetes.io/zone\" (cross-reference; region is a larger domain made up of zones)\n\n**4. `kubernetes.io/os` and `kubernetes.io/arch`**\n- Used on: Node, Pod (for `kubernetes.io/os`)\n- Description: Kubelet populates these with Go runtime values (`runtime.GOOS`, `runtime.GOARCH`) to support heterogeneous clusters.\n\n**5. `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix**\n- NOT PRESENT in the provided document content.\n\n**6. `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable`**\n- Type: Taint\n- Description: \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid race condition.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5de4450-c1f8-40eb-9c44-c8ddc092eae4","uuid":"b0f12473-6d9f-4ef3-a6b7-7d9c3f1f9f4b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T13:41:11.400Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":119528,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Kubernetes Well-Known Labels and Taints - Targeted Entries\n\n**1. `kubernetes.io/hostname`**\n- Used on: Node\n- Description: \"The Kubelet populates this label with the hostname of the node.\"\n\n**2. `topology.kubernetes.io/zone`**\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- Description: \"A zone represents a logical failure domain\" used by the kubelet or cloud-controller-manager.\n\n**3. `topology.kubernetes.io/region`**\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- Description: \"See topology.kubernetes.io/zone\" (cross-reference; region is a larger domain made up of zones)\n\n**4. `kubernetes.io/os` and `kubernetes.io/arch`**\n- Used on: Node, Pod (for `kubernetes.io/os`)\n- Description: Kubelet populates these with Go runtime values (`runtime.GOOS`, `runtime.GOARCH`) to support heterogeneous clusters.\n\n**5. `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix**\n- NOT PRESENT in the provided document content.\n\n**6. `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable`**\n- Type: Taint\n- Description: \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid race condition.\"","durationMs":4454,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/_index.md"}}
